# K03 (Codex K03-NS-ROLES-NEXT-20261007-09, -07 Q2; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md:666, :668): a named Structure is
# visible throughout the unit both ways, so a head that names one is known before its tail is read, whatever the
# tail is written as.
# Control: with no other Later in the unit, `Later: 3` defines Later (its retained body is 3, S5); m reads nothing of
# it and exits 7.
Later: 3
fn: m () int
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
